EmailWithName: every form its examples take (area 19, "Changing a standard type's encoding")
encoding 1
column name text
column address text

example Mary Somerville <mary@example.com>
text Mary Somerville <mary@example.com>
json {"name":"Mary Somerville","address":"mary@example.com"}
stored name 'Mary Somerville'
stored address 'mary@example.com'

example "Somerville, Mary" <mary@example.com>
text "Somerville, Mary" <mary@example.com>
json {"name":"Somerville, Mary","address":"mary@example.com"}
stored name 'Somerville, Mary'
stored address 'mary@example.com'

example mary@example.com
text mary@example.com
json {"name":null,"address":"mary@example.com"}
stored name NULL::text
stored address 'mary@example.com'
